+        " fill="currentColor"></path></g></svg></div></div><div class="sc-eulNck jDHlIl api-content"><div class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy api-info"><h1 class="sc-imWYAI sc-ktJbId liqgno kxOCzH">Todoist API <span>(1)</span></h1><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct"></div><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct" data-role="redoc-summary"></div><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct" data-role="redoc-description"></div></div></div></div><div id="section/Developing-with-Todoist" data-section-id="section/Developing-with-Todoist" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-jXbUNg kCMUHi"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#section/Developing-with-Todoist" aria-label="section/Developing-with-Todoist"></a>Developing with Todoist</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Thanks for your interest in developing apps with Todoist. In this section
+we will provide an overview of the API we offer and cover some common topics for
+application development using them.</p>
+<p>You can use our API for free, but depending on your Todoist account plan (or that of the authenticated user), some
+features may be restricted.</p>
+<p>Please consider subscribing to the <a href="https://groups.google.com/a/doist.com/g/todoist-api">Todoist API mailing
+list</a> to get important updates.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-API" data-section-id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-API" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-API" aria-label="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-API"></a>Our API</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Our API uses an approach that should be familiar to anyone with experience
+calling <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Representational_state_transfer">RESTful</a> APIs.</p>
+<p>We also have a special endpoint called <code>/sync</code>, which is used by our
+first-party clients to keep the data updated locally without having to make many
+separate requests to the API. Anyone can use it, and some actions will only be
+available via <code>/sync</code>. The format is unconventional compared to current API standards,
+but it is our main driver for first-party apps.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-SDKs" data-section-id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-SDKs" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-SDKs" aria-label="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Our-SDKs"></a>Our SDKs</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Our Python and JavaScript SDKs streamline working with the Todoist API, and
+can be installed from the main package registries for each ecosystem.</p>
+<p>For instructions, examples, and reference documentation, visit their pages:</p>
+<ul>
+<li><a href="https://doist.github.io/todoist-api-python/">Todoist Python SDK</a></li>
+<li><a href="https://doist.github.io/todoist-sdk-typescript/">Todoist TypeScript SDK</a></li>
+</ul>
+</div></div></div><div id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Resource-IDs-and-optimistic-updates" data-section-id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Resource-IDs-and-optimistic-updates" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#section/Developing-with-Todoist/Resource-IDs-and-optimistic-updates" aria-label="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Resource-IDs-and-optimistic-updates"></a>Resource IDs and optimistic updates</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Our first-party clients use optimistic updates so newly-created resources
+(tasks, projects, etc.) are usable in the UI before the server has confirmed
+them. During that window, the resource is referenced by a <strong>client-side
+placeholder ID</strong> with a <code>tmp-</code> prefix — for example
+<code>tmp-UUID-XXXX-UnixMillis</code>. Once the sync with Todoist completes, the client
+replaces the placeholder with the real server-assigned ID.</p>
+<p><strong>Placeholder IDs are not valid server-side resource identifiers.</strong> If you
+pass a <code>tmp-</code>-prefixed ID to a REST endpoint, the request will fail with a
+validation error (for example <code>Non-base32 digit found</code>) because the API only
+accepts base32-encoded or numeric IDs (depending on the resource).</p>
+<p>If your integration receives a resource ID from a client context (e.g. a UI
+extension payload or a browser event fired right after task creation), you
+should:</p>
+<ol>
+<li><strong>Detect placeholder IDs early</strong> — any ID starting with <code>tmp-</code> has not
+yet synced.</li>
+<li><strong>Wait for sync to complete before calling the REST API.</strong> First-party
+clients expose the real ID once the next <code>/sync</code> round-trip returns
+(see the <a href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Sync/Overview/Temporary-resource-ID"><code>temp_id_mapping</code></a>
+field in the Sync API response).</li>
+<li><strong>Retry your API call with the confirmed ID</strong> once available. If you
+cannot wait, surface the delay to the end user rather than calling the
+REST API with the placeholder.</li>
+</ol>
+<p>Note that this client-side <code>tmp-</code>-prefixed placeholder is distinct from the
+<code>temp_id</code> used in Sync API commands — the latter is a developer-supplied
+UUID that the server resolves inside a single <code>/sync</code> request. See the
+<a href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Sync/Overview/Temporary-resource-ID">Sync API's Temporary resource ID documentation</a>
+for details on <code>temp_id</code> and <code>temp_id_mapping</code>.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Integrations" data-section-id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Integrations" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#section/Developing-with-Todoist/Integrations" aria-label="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Integrations"></a>Integrations</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Integrations can be created and updated <a href="https://app.todoist.com/app/settings/integrations/app-management">here</a>.</p>
+<p>Once done, they can also be submitted for evaluation and inclusion in <a href="https://www.todoist.com/integrations">our
+official integrations list</a>. This not
+only serves as an opportunity to market your integration to our audience, but
+will also serve as a way to help users get set up and familiar with your app quickly.</p>
+<p>For more information on how to submit your integration for evaluation, refer to our <a href="https://www.todoist.com/help/articles/marketing-your-todoist-integration-B6C5sCKkn">Marketing your integration page</a>.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Brand-usage" data-section-id="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Brand-usage" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#section/Developing-with-Todoist/Brand-usage" aria-label="section/Developing-with-Todoist/Brand-usage"></a>Brand usage</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>When creating with the Todoist platform, you may reference Todoist to describe
+what your app does, but you must keep it clearly distinct from Todoist's official
+products.</p>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Naming:</strong> "Todoist" cannot be the primary name of your app. Use a format
+that signals independence, such as "x for Todoist" or "x with Todoist".</li>
+<li><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Your application description must state that it is "not
+created by, affiliated with, or supported by Todoist."</li>
+<li><strong>Logo and branding:</strong> Any use of Todoist's marks must comply with our
+<a href="https://doist.com/brand-assets/todoist-logo.zip">brand guidelines</a>, which are
+available for download.</li>
+<li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> By using Todoist branding you agree to follow our brand
+guidelines and <a href="https://www.todoist.com/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>For detailed questions about using the Todoist marks, contact
+<a href="mailto:press@doist.com">press@doist.com</a>.</p>
+<p>Lost? <a href="https://www.todoist.com/contact/login?returnTo=%2Fcontact">Reach out to us</a> anytime.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-CLI" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-CLI" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-jXbUNg kCMUHi"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-CLI" aria-label="tag/Todoist-CLI"></a>Todoist CLI</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Use Todoist from your terminal with the official, open-source
+<a href="https://www.todoist.com/cli">Todoist CLI</a>. It is useful for quick task capture,
+terminal workflows, local scripts, and giving AI coding agents access to the
+same task list you use in Todoist.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Installation" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Installation" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-CLI/Installation" aria-label="tag/Todoist-CLI/Installation"></a>Installation</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Install the npm package:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-shell"><span class="token function">npm</span> <span class="token function">install</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-g</span> @doist/todoist-cli
+</code></pre>
+<p>Then authenticate with Todoist:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">td auth login
+</code></pre>
+<p>This opens your browser to authenticate with Todoist. Once approved, the token
+is stored in your operating system credential manager.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Common-commands" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Common-commands" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-CLI/Common-commands" aria-label="tag/Todoist-CLI/Common-commands"></a>Common commands</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><pre><code class="language-shell">td <span class="token function">add</span> <span class="token string">"Buy milk tomorrow #Shopping"</span>
+td today
+td inbox
+td task list
+td task list <span class="token parameter variable">--project</span> <span class="token string">"Work"</span>
+td project list
+</code></pre>
+<p>Run <code>td --help</code> or <code>td &lt;command&gt; --help</code> for the full command reference.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Agent-skills" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Agent-skills" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-CLI/Agent-skills" aria-label="tag/Todoist-CLI/Agent-skills"></a>Agent skills</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>The CLI can install maintained skills for coding agents:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">td skill <span class="token function">install</span> claude-code
+td skill <span class="token function">install</span> codex
+td skill <span class="token function">install</span> copilot
+td skill <span class="token function">install</span> cursor
+td skill <span class="token function">install</span> gemini
+td skill <span class="token function">install</span> pi
+td skill <span class="token function">install</span> universal
+</code></pre>
+<p>Use <code>td skill list</code> to see installed skills and <code>td skill uninstall &lt;agent&gt;</code> to
+remove one.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Shell-completions" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-CLI/Shell-completions" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-CLI/Shell-completions" aria-label="tag/Todoist-CLI/Shell-completions"></a>Shell completions</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Tab completion is available for bash, zsh, and fish:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">td completion <span class="token function">install</span>
+td completion <span class="token function">install</span> <span class="token function">zsh</span>
+</code></pre>
+<p>For source code, issues, releases, and contribution details, visit the
+<a href="https://github.com/Doist/todoist-cli">Doist/todoist-cli repository</a>.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-MCP" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-MCP" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-jXbUNg kCMUHi"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-MCP" aria-label="tag/Todoist-MCP"></a>Todoist MCP</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Integrate AI assistants with Todoist using the <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/">Model Context Protocol</a> (MCP), an open standard for secure access to your tasks and projects. Our hosted MCP server works with Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and VS Code.</p>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Easy setup:</strong> OAuth in a minute.  </li>
+<li><strong>Full access:</strong> Read, create, and update your tasks &amp; projects.  </li>
+<li><strong>Use cases:</strong> Daily reviews, project planning, natural-language queries.</li>
+</ul>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-MCP/Setup-guide" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-MCP/Setup-guide" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-MCP/Setup-guide" aria-label="tag/Todoist-MCP/Setup-guide"></a>Setup guide</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p><strong>Primary URL (Streamable HTTP):</strong></p>
+<p><code>https://ai.todoist.net/mcp</code></p>
+<h3 id="claude">Claude</h3>
+<ol>
+<li>Open <strong>Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector</strong>.  </li>
+<li>Enter <code>https://ai.todoist.net/mcp</code> and complete OAuth.</li>
+</ol>
+<h3 id="cursor">Cursor</h3>
+<p>Create <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code> (global) or <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> (project):</p>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+  <span class="token string-property property">"mcpServers"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"todoist"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"command"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"npx"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"args"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">"-y"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">"mcp-remote"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">"https://ai.todoist.net/mcp"</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span>
+    <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<p>Then enable the server in Cursor settings if prompted.</p>
+<h3 id="claude-code-cli">Claude Code (CLI)</h3>
+<pre><code class="language-bash">claude mcp <span class="token function">add</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--transport</span> http todoist https://ai.todoist.net/mcp
+</code></pre>
+<h3 id="visual-studio-code">Visual Studio Code</h3>
+<p>Command Palette → MCP: Add Server → Type HTTP and use:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+  <span class="token string-property property">"servers"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"todoist"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"type"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"http"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"url"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"https://ai.todoist.net/mcp"</span>
+    <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<h3 id="other-clients">Other Clients</h3>
+<p><code>npx -y mcp-remote https://ai.todoist.net/mcp</code></p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Todoist-MCP/Tool-response-format" data-section-id="tag/Todoist-MCP/Tool-response-format" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Todoist-MCP/Tool-response-format" aria-label="tag/Todoist-MCP/Tool-response-format"></a>Tool response format</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>Every <code>tools/call</code> response from the Todoist MCP server includes the same data in three forms. This mirrors the standard MCP tool result shape, but it is worth calling out because different MCP clients expose different parts of it to the model or to the calling application.</p>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+  <span class="token string-property property">"result"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"content"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>
+      <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+        <span class="token string-property property">"type"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"text"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+        <span class="token string-property property">"text"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"{\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"...\",\"content\":\"...\",\"priority\":4},...],\"totalCount\":2,\"hasMore\":false,\"appliedFilters\":{\"limit\":10,\"filter\":\"today\"}}"</span>
+      <span class="token punctuation">}</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+      <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+        <span class="token string-property property">"type"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"text"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+        <span class="token string-property property">"text"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"Tasks matching filter: today: 2 (limit 10).\nFilter: filter: today."</span>
+      <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+    <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"structuredContent"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"tasks"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span>
+        <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token string-property property">"id"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"..."</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string-property property">"content"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"..."</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string-property property">"priority"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">4</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+      <span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"totalCount"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">2</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"hasMore"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token boolean">false</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+      <span class="token string-property property">"appliedFilters"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span> <span class="token string-property property">"limit"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">10</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string-property property">"filter"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"today"</span> <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+    <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+  <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<h3 id="fields">Fields</h3>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Stringified JSON of <code>structuredContent</code></strong> — included as a <code>text</code> content item, for compatibility with clients that surface text content but do not yet expose <code>structuredContent</code>. For tools that only return text and structured data (the majority of Todoist tools) this is <code>content[0]</code>. For tools that also return non-text content items such as images or embedded resources (for example, <code>view-attachment</code>), those tool-authored items come first and the JSON <code>text</code> item follows them.</li>
+<li><strong>Human-readable summary</strong> — always the <strong>last</strong> <code>text</code> content item in the <code>content[]</code> array. Intended for display to end users or for models that only consume text. Not intended to be parsed.</li>
+<li><strong><code>structuredContent</code></strong> — the same payload as the JSON <code>text</code> item, already parsed as a JSON object. Available to clients implementing MCP spec revision <code>2025-03-26</code> or later.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>The JSON <code>text</code> item and <code>structuredContent</code> always contain the same data. The trailing summary is derived from that data and is not intended to be parsed.</p>
+<h3 id="which-field-should-you-consume">Which field should you consume?</h3>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Direct JSON-RPC callers:</strong> prefer <code>structuredContent</code>. If your client targets an older MCP spec revision, parse the JSON <code>text</code> item — locate it by checking each <code>text</code> content item for a JSON payload rather than by hard-coded index.</li>
+<li><strong>Callers routing through an AI orchestration layer</strong> (for example, the OpenAI Responses API, an agent framework, or another LLM client): check which content items that layer surfaces back to you. Some clients pass through all parts of the tool response; others expose only the first content item.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3 id="client-compatibility-note">Client compatibility note</h3>
+<p>If two MCP clients appear to receive different data from the same Todoist tool call, the difference is almost always in how the client surfaces the response — not in what the server returns. The Todoist MCP server returns the same <code>content[]</code> array and <code>structuredContent</code> object to every caller.</p>
+<p>For example:</p>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>Claude</strong> and <strong>Claude Code</strong> process all content items and <code>structuredContent</code>, so the model has access to the full structured payload.</li>
+<li>The <strong>OpenAI Responses API</strong> surfaces only <code>content[0]</code> to the caller and strips <code>structuredContent</code>. For tools that return only text and structured data, <code>content[0]</code> is the stringified JSON payload and callers can parse it directly. For tools that also return non-text content items (for example, <code>view-attachment</code> returning an image), <code>content[0]</code> is the tool-authored item; callers needing the structured payload from those tools should access the server via direct JSON-RPC.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>If you are debugging unexpected output, inspect the raw JSON-RPC response from <code>ai.todoist.net/mcp</code> before assuming a server-side difference.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Authorization" data-section-id="tag/Authorization" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-jXbUNg kCMUHi"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Authorization" aria-label="tag/Authorization"></a>Authorization</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><blockquote class="lang-specific shell">
+    <p>An authenticated request with authorization header:</p>
+</blockquote>
+
+<pre><code class="language-shell">$ <span class="token function">curl</span> https://api.todoist.com/api/v1/sync <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-H</span> <span class="token string">"Authorization: Bearer 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token assign-left variable">sync_token</span><span class="token operator">=</span><span class="token string">'*'</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token assign-left variable">resource_types</span><span class="token operator">=</span><span class="token string">'["all"]'</span>
+</code></pre>
+<p>In order to make authorized calls to the Sync API, your application must provide
+an <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Authorization">authorization
+header</a>
+with the appropriate <code>Bearer $token</code>. For working through the examples, you can
+obtain your personal API token from the <a href="https://app.todoist.com/app/settings/integrations">integrations
+settings</a> for your account.</p>
+<p>To authenticate other users, your application will need to obtain a token from
+them using the OAuth protocol. For information on how to obtain a token from our
+service using OAuth, please see the <a href="https://developer.todoist.com/guides/#authorization">authorization
+guide</a>.</p>
+<p>For the sake of simplicity the token is not listed on every parameter table but
+please note that the <strong>token parameter is required for every resource</strong>.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Authorization/OAuth" data-section-id="tag/Authorization/OAuth" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Authorization/OAuth" aria-label="tag/Authorization/OAuth"></a>OAuth</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><p>OAuth is also available for token generation. It's especially useful for
+external applications to obtain a user authorized API token via the OAuth2
+protocol. Before getting started, developers need to create their applications
+in the <a href="https://app.todoist.com/app/settings/integrations/app-management">App Management Console</a>
+and configure one or more valid OAuth2 redirect URLs. A registered Todoist
+application is assigned a unique <code>Client ID</code> and <code>Client Secret</code> which are
+needed for the OAuth2 flow.</p>
+<p>This procedure is comprised of 3 steps.</p>
+<h3 id="step-1-authorization-request">Step 1: Authorization request</h3>
+<blockquote>
+<p>An example of the URL to the authorization endpoint:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">https://app.todoist.com/oauth/authorize?client_id<span class="token operator">=</span>0123456789abcdef<span class="token operator">&amp;</span><span class="token assign-left variable">scope</span><span class="token operator">=</span>data:read,data:delete<span class="token operator">&amp;</span><span class="token assign-left variable">state</span><span class="token operator">=</span>secretstring<span class="token operator">&amp;</span><span class="token assign-left variable">response_type</span><span class="token operator">=</span>code
+</code></pre>
+<p>Redirect users to the authorization URL at the endpoint
+<code>https://app.todoist.com/oauth/authorize</code>, with the specified request parameters.</p>
+<h4 id="required-parameters">Required parameters</h4>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Name</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>client_id</td>
+<td>The unique Client ID of the Todoist application that you registered.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>scope</td>
+<td>A comma separated list of permissions that you would like the users to grant to your application. See the below table for detail on the available scopes.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>state</td>
+<td>A unique and unguessable string. It is used to protect you against cross-site request forgery attacks.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h4 id="optional-parameters">Optional parameters</h4>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Name</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>redirect_uri</td>
+<td>The redirect URL for your application. If your application has multiple redirect URIs configured, this parameter is <strong>required</strong> — the request will be rejected with <code>invalid_request</code> if it is omitted.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>response_type</td>
+<td>Todoist supports the authorization code flow. This parameter may be omitted or set to <code>code</code>. Other values are rejected with <code>unsupported_response_type</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h4 id="permission-scopes">Permission scopes</h4>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Name</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>task:add</td>
+<td>Grants permission to add new tasks (the application cannot read or modify any existing data).</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>data:read</td>
+<td>Grants read-only access to application data, including tasks, projects, labels, and filters.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>data:read_write</td>
+<td>Grants read and write access to application data, including tasks, projects, labels, and filters. This scope includes <code>task:add</code> and <code>data:read</code> scopes.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>data:delete</td>
+<td>Grants permission to delete application data, including tasks, labels, and filters.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>project:delete</td>
+<td>Grants permission to delete projects.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>backups:read</td>
+<td>Grants permission to list backups with <code>GET /api/v1/backups</code> without MFA. Downloading a backup with <code>GET /api/v1/backups/download</code> still requires <code>data:read_write</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h4 id="potential-errors">Potential errors</h4>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Error</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>User Rejected Authorization Request</td>
+<td>When the user denies your authorization request, Todoist will redirect the user to the configured redirect URI with the <code>error</code> parameter: <code>http://example.com?error=access_denied</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Redirect URI Not Configured</td>
+<td>This JSON error will be returned to the requester (your user's browser) if redirect URI is not configured in the App Management Console.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Invalid Application Status</td>
+<td>When your application exceeds the maximum token limit or when your application is being suspended due to abuse, Todoist will redirect the user to the configured redirect URI with the <code>error</code> parameter: <code>http://example.com?error=invalid_application_status</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Invalid Scope</td>
+<td>When the <code>scope</code> parameter is invalid, Todoist will redirect the user to the configured redirect URI with <code>error</code> parameter: <code>http://example.com?error=invalid_scope</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Unsupported Response Type</td>
+<td>When the <code>response_type</code> parameter is set to a value other than <code>code</code>, Todoist will redirect the user to the configured redirect URI with <code>error</code> parameter: <code>http://example.com?error=unsupported_response_type</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h3 id="step-2-redirection-to-your-application-site">Step 2: Redirection to your application site</h3>
+<p>When the user grants your authorization request, the user will be redirected to
+the redirect URL configured for your application. The redirect request
+will come with two query parameters attached: <code>code</code> and <code>state</code>.</p>
+<p>The <code>code</code> parameter contains the authorization code that you will use to
+exchange for an access token. The <code>state</code> parameter should match the <code>state</code>
+parameter that you supplied in the previous step. If the <code>state</code> is unmatched,
+your request has been compromised by other parties, and the process should be
+aborted.</p>
+<h3 id="step-3-token-exchange">Step 3: Token exchange</h3>
+<blockquote>
+<p>An example of exchanging the token:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">$ <span class="token function">curl</span> <span class="token string">"https://api.todoist.com/oauth/access_token"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"client_id=0123456789abcdef"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"client_secret=secret"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"code=abcdef"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"redirect_uri=https://example.com"</span>
+</code></pre>
+<blockquote>
+<p>On success, Todoist returns HTTP 200 with the token in JSON object format. For
+applications with refresh tokens enabled (the default for newly-created apps),
+the response also includes <code>expires_in</code> and <code>refresh_token</code>:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"access_token"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"token_type"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"Bearer"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"expires_in"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">3600</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"refresh_token"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"scope"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"data:read_write"</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<blockquote>
+<p>Legacy applications without refresh tokens enabled receive a response whose
+<code>expires_in</code> is a 10-year compatibility value (<code>315360000</code>) rather than a
+meaningful expiry, and no <code>refresh_token</code>. These access tokens are long-lived
+and will continue to work:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"access_token"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"token_type"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"Bearer"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"expires_in"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">315360000</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<p>Once you have the authorization <code>code</code>, you can exchange it for the access token
+by sending a <code>POST</code> request to the following endpoint:</p>
+<p><code>https://api.todoist.com/oauth/access_token</code>.</p>
+<h4 id="required-parameters-1">Required parameters</h4>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Name</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>client_id</td>
+<td>The Client ID of the Todoist application that you registered.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>client_secret</td>
+<td>The Client Secret of the Todoist application that you registered.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>code</td>
+<td>The code that was sent in the query string to the redirect URL in the previous step.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h4 id="potential-errors-1">Potential errors</h4>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Error</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>Bad Authorization Code Error</td>
+<td>Occurs when the <code>code</code> parameter does not match the code that is given in the redirect request: <code>{"error": "bad_authorization_code"}</code></td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Incorrect Client Credentials Error</td>
+<td>Occurs when the <code>client_id</code> or <code>client_secret</code> parameters are incorrect: <code>{"error": "incorrect_application_credentials"}</code></td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Authorization/Dynamic-Client-Registration" data-section-id="tag/Authorization/Dynamic-Client-Registration" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Authorization/Dynamic-Client-Registration" aria-label="tag/Authorization/Dynamic-Client-Registration"></a>Dynamic Client Registration</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><blockquote>
+<p>Registering a new dynamic client:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">$ <span class="token function">curl</span> <span class="token string">"https://api.todoist.com/oauth/register"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-H</span> <span class="token string">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">'{
+        "client_name": "My App",
+        "redirect_uris": ["https://example.com/callback"],
+        "scope": "data:read_write",
+        "grant_types": ["authorization_code", "refresh_token"],
+        "response_types": ["code"],
+        "token_endpoint_auth_method": "client_secret_post"
+    }'</span>
+</code></pre>
+<blockquote>
+<p>On success, Todoist returns HTTP 201 Created with a newly-issued
+client in <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7591">RFC 7591</a>
+format. The response includes <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code> and
+<code>Pragma: no-cache</code> headers, also per RFC 7591 §3.2.1:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"client_id"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"tdd_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"client_secret"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"client_name"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"My App"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"redirect_uris"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">"https://example.com/callback"</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"scope"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"data:read_write"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"grant_types"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">"authorization_code"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">"refresh_token"</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"response_types"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">"code"</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"token_endpoint_auth_method"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"client_secret_post"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"client_id_issued_at"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">1776865756</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"client_secret_expires_at"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">0</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<p>Clients that cannot pre-register through the App Management Console —
+notably multi-tenant integrations, MCP servers, and AI agents acting on
+behalf of an end user — can register themselves at runtime via
+<a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7591">RFC 7591</a>.</p>
+<p>Send a <code>POST</code> to <code>https://api.todoist.com/oauth/register</code> with a JSON
+body describing the client. No authentication is required, but the
+endpoint is rate limited per caller.</p>
+<h3 id="request-parameters">Request parameters</h3>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Name</th>
+<th>Required</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>redirect_uris</td>
+<td>Yes</td>
+<td>Array of redirect URIs. Up to 10 entries, each ≤512 characters. Must be HTTPS (localhost is allowed for testing).</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>client_name</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Human-readable name shown on the consent screen.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>client_uri</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Public URL for the application.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>logo_uri</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Public URL for the application logo.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>scope</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Space-separated scopes the client will request. Restricted scopes are rejected. Defaults to <code>data:read_write</code> when omitted.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>grant_types</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Array of supported grant types. Must include <code>authorization_code</code>. Include <code>refresh_token</code> to use token refresh. Defaults to <code>["authorization_code"]</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>response_types</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Array of supported response types. Must include <code>code</code>. Defaults to <code>["code"]</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>token_endpoint_auth_method</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>One of <code>client_secret_post</code> (default), <code>client_secret_basic</code>, or <code>none</code> (public client using PKCE).</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h3 id="response">Response</h3>
+<p>Dynamic clients are identified by a <code>tdd_</code> prefix on <code>client_id</code>. The
+<code>client_secret_expires_at</code> field is <code>0</code> — client secrets do not expire.
+Use the returned credentials with the standard
+<a href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#step-1-authorization-request">authorization code flow</a> above.</p>
+<h3 id="potential-errors">Potential errors</h3>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Error</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>Invalid Client Metadata</td>
+<td>A field failed validation — e.g. a redirect URI is malformed or not HTTPS, or <code>grant_types</code> omits <code>authorization_code</code>: <code>{"error": "invalid_client_metadata"}</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Invalid Scope</td>
+<td>A requested scope is unknown or restricted to first-party use: <code>{"error": "invalid_scope"}</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Rate Limit Exceeded</td>
+<td>Too many registration requests in a short period; retry later.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Authorization/OAuth-Client-ID-Metadata-Document" data-section-id="tag/Authorization/OAuth-Client-ID-Metadata-Document" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Authorization/OAuth-Client-ID-Metadata-Document" aria-label="tag/Authorization/OAuth-Client-ID-Metadata-Document"></a>OAuth Client ID Metadata Document</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><blockquote>
+<p>Example metadata document hosted by the client at its <code>client_id</code> URL:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"client_id"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"https://example.com/oauth-client-metadata.json"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"client_name"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"My App"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"redirect_uris"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">"https://example.com/callback"</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"grant_types"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">"authorization_code"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">"refresh_token"</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"response_types"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token string">"code"</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"token_endpoint_auth_method"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"none"</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<p>As an alternative to RFC 7591 registration, Todoist supports
+<a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document/">OAuth Client ID Metadata Documents</a>
+— a zero-registration flow in which the <code>client_id</code> itself is an HTTPS
+URL pointing to a JSON metadata document describing the client. The
+authorization server fetches and validates the document on demand, so
+clients don't pre-register at all.</p>
+<p>This is intended for public clients that cannot safely store a
+<code>client_secret</code> (browser-based SPAs, desktop apps, MCP servers). Clients
+protect themselves with PKCE during the authorization code exchange
+instead of a client secret.</p>
+<h3 id="hosting-the-document">Hosting the document</h3>
+<p>Host a JSON document at an HTTPS URL you control. The URL must:</p>
+<ul>
+<li>use the <code>https://</code> scheme (no plaintext HTTP)</li>
+<li>include a path component beyond <code>/</code> (e.g. <code>/oauth/client.json</code>)</li>
+<li>resolve to a publicly routable IP address (private and loopback ranges are rejected for SSRF protection)</li>
+</ul>
+<p>Todoist enforces a <strong>5KB maximum size</strong> and a <strong>5-second fetch timeout</strong>
+on the document. Redirects are not followed.</p>
+<h3 id="document-fields">Document fields</h3>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Field</th>
+<th>Required</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>client_id</td>
+<td>Yes</td>
+<td>Must exactly match the URL the document was fetched from.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>redirect_uris</td>
+<td>Yes</td>
+<td>Non-empty array of redirect URIs. Must be HTTPS (localhost allowed for testing).</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>token_endpoint_auth_method</td>
+<td>Yes</td>
+<td>Must be <code>"none"</code>. Metadata clients are public clients by design and cannot hold a symmetric secret.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>grant_types</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Defaults to <code>["authorization_code"]</code>. Include <code>"refresh_token"</code> to use refresh.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>response_types</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Defaults to <code>["code"]</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>client_name</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Human-readable name shown on the consent screen.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>client_uri</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Public URL for the application.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>logo_uri</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Public URL for the application logo.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>scope</td>
+<td>No</td>
+<td>Space-separated scopes the client will request.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h3 id="using-the-metadata-document">Using the metadata document</h3>
+<p>Pass the document URL as the <code>client_id</code> on the
+<a href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#step-1-authorization-request">authorization request</a>. Todoist fetches
+and caches the document, validates it, and proceeds with the
+authorization code flow as usual. Because metadata clients use
+<code>token_endpoint_auth_method: none</code>, the <code>client_secret</code> parameter is
+<strong>not sent</strong> on the <code>/oauth/access_token</code> exchange. Clients must
+additionally send PKCE parameters (<code>code_challenge</code> on the authorization
+request, <code>code_verifier</code> on the token exchange).</p>
+<h3 id="refreshing-the-document">Refreshing the document</h3>
+<p>Metadata documents are cached server-side. Changes to the document are
+picked up on the next cache miss, which happens automatically — there is
+no explicit refresh endpoint. To force a refresh you can revoke the
+client via the <a href="https://app.todoist.com/app/settings/integrations/app-management">App Management Console</a>;
+the next authorization attempt will fetch fresh metadata.</p>
+<h3 id="potential-errors">Potential errors</h3>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Error</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>Invalid Client</td>
+<td>The document URL failed SSRF validation (HTTP, private IP, missing path), the document is malformed, exceeds the size limit, or <code>client_id</code> inside the document does not match the URL: <code>{"error": "invalid_client"}</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Rate Limit Exceeded</td>
+<td>Too many metadata document fetches in a short period; retry later.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Authorization/Refreshing-access-tokens" data-section-id="tag/Authorization/Refreshing-access-tokens" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Authorization/Refreshing-access-tokens" aria-label="tag/Authorization/Refreshing-access-tokens"></a>Refreshing access tokens</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><blockquote>
+<p>Exchanging a refresh token for a new access token:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">$ <span class="token function">curl</span> <span class="token string">"https://api.todoist.com/oauth/access_token"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"client_id=0123456789abcdef"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"client_secret=secret"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"grant_type=refresh_token"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-d</span> <span class="token string">"refresh_token=abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01"</span>
+</code></pre>
+<blockquote>
+<p>On success, Todoist returns HTTP 200 with a new access token and a rotated
+refresh token:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-json"><span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"access_token"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210fedcba98"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"token_type"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"Bearer"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"expires_in"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">3600</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"refresh_token"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"9876543210abcdef9876543210abcdef98765432"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"scope"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"data:read_write"</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+</code></pre>
+<h3 id="which-applications-issue-refresh-tokens">Which applications issue refresh tokens?</h3>
+<p>Refresh tokens are <strong>enabled by default for newly-created applications</strong>. Access
+tokens issued to these applications expire one hour after they are issued, and
+clients must exchange the refresh token for a new access token to continue
+making requests.</p>
+<p>Legacy applications created before refresh tokens were introduced continue to
+receive long-lived access tokens that do not expire. These applications can
+opt in to refresh tokens via the
+<a href="https://app.todoist.com/app/settings/integrations/app-management">App Management Console</a>.
+Once enabled, the setting cannot be disabled — all new tokens issued by the
+application will follow the refresh flow. Tokens issued before opting in remain
+long-lived and are not retroactively converted.</p>
+<h3 id="how-to-refresh">How to refresh</h3>
+<p>To exchange a refresh token for a new access token, send a <code>POST</code> request to
+<code>https://api.todoist.com/oauth/access_token</code> with the following parameters:</p>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Name</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>client_id</td>
+<td>The Client ID of the Todoist application.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>grant_type</td>
+<td>Must be the literal string <code>refresh_token</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>refresh_token</td>
+<td>The refresh token received in the previous token exchange or refresh.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>client_secret</td>
+<td>The Client Secret of the Todoist application. Required for confidential clients — see <em>Client authentication</em> below.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h4 id="client-authentication">Client authentication</h4>
+<p>Todoist's token endpoint supports three authentication methods, matching the
+<code>token_endpoint_auth_method</code> chosen when the application was registered:</p>
+<ul>
+<li><code>client_secret_post</code> (default for confidential clients) — <code>client_id</code> and
+<code>client_secret</code> sent in the request body.</li>
+<li><code>client_secret_basic</code> — credentials sent via HTTP Basic auth:
+<code>Authorization: Basic base64(client_id:client_secret)</code>.</li>
+<li><code>none</code> — public clients (including clients registered via the OAuth 2.0
+Client ID Metadata Document flow). <code>client_secret</code> is not sent or validated;
+these clients are expected to protect themselves with PKCE during the
+authorization code exchange.</li>
+</ul>
+<h4 id="optional-parameters">Optional parameters</h4>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Name</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>scope</td>
+<td>A comma separated subset of the originally granted scopes. Clients may request a narrower set of scopes; requesting scopes beyond the original grant returns an error.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<h3 id="token-rotation-and-security">Token rotation and security</h3>
+<p>Refresh tokens are <strong>rotated on every successful refresh</strong>. The refresh token
+returned in the response replaces the one you just used, which is marked as
+consumed. Always store the latest refresh token from each response.</p>
+<h4 id="network-retries-inside-the-grace-window">Network retries inside the grace window</h4>
+<p>If the same (already-consumed) refresh token is presented again within 60
+seconds of being consumed, Todoist treats the second call as a legitimate
+network retry rather than token reuse. The response returns HTTP <code>200</code> with
+the <strong>same replacement access token</strong> that was issued by the original
+successful refresh, but <strong>omits the <code>refresh_token</code> field</strong> (Todoist cannot
+reissue it from the consumed hash). Clients must therefore retain the
+refresh token from the original <code>200</code> response; they cannot recover it from
+a grace-window retry.</p>
+<h4 id="replay-detection-outside-the-grace-window">Replay detection outside the grace window</h4>
+<p>If a consumed refresh token is presented outside the 60-second grace window,
+Todoist treats it as a potential replay attack. All access and refresh tokens
+issued to the user for the application are revoked, and the user must
+re-authorize the application.</p>
+<h3 id="detecting-an-expired-access-token">Detecting an expired access token</h3>
+<p>When an access token is invalid or has expired, API requests using that token
+return HTTP <code>401 Unauthorized</code> with Todoist's standard <code>UNAUTHORIZED</code>
+(<code>error_code</code> <code>477</code>) JSON body and an <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6750">RFC 6750</a>
+<code>WWW-Authenticate</code> challenge. The response may also include retry backoff
+metadata:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-http"><span class="token response-status"><span class="token http-version property">HTTP/1.1</span> <span class="token status-code number">401</span> <span class="token reason-phrase string">Unauthorized</span></span>
+<span class="token header"><span class="token header-name keyword">Content-Type</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token header-value">application/json</span></span>
+<span class="token header"><span class="token header-name keyword">Retry-After</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token header-value">3</span></span>
+<span class="token header"><span class="token header-name keyword">WWW-Authenticate</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span> <span class="token header-value">Bearer error="invalid_token", error_description="Unauthorized", resource_metadata="https://api.todoist.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource"</span></span>
+<span class="token application-json">
+<span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"error_tag"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"UNAUTHORIZED"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"error_code"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">477</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"error"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"Unauthorized"</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"http_code"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">401</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+    <span class="token string-property property">"error_extra"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span>
+        <span class="token string-property property">"retry_after"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token number">3</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span>
+        <span class="token string-property property">"event_id"</span><span class="token operator">:</span> <span class="token string">"&lt;hash&gt;"</span>
+    <span class="token punctuation">}</span>
+<span class="token punctuation">}</span></span>
+</code></pre>
+<p>Clients should treat this response as a signal to refresh the access token and
+retry the original request with the new token. When present, <code>retry_after</code> and
+the <code>Retry-After</code> header are backoff metadata; do not wait and retry the same
+invalid or expired token. For legacy applications without refresh tokens
+enabled, the user must re-authorize the application instead. The
+<code>resource_metadata</code> URL points at an
+<a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9728">RFC 9728</a> Protected Resource
+Metadata document that identifies the authorization server, which is useful for
+clients discovering the refresh endpoint automatically.</p>
+<h3 id="potential-errors">Potential errors</h3>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Error</th>
+<th>Description</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody><tr>
+<td>Invalid Grant</td>
+<td>The refresh token is unknown, expired, revoked, or has already been consumed outside the grace window: <code>{"error": "invalid_grant"}</code>. The user must re-authorize the application. Also returned for legacy applications that have not opted in to refresh tokens, because they have no refresh token to present.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Invalid Client</td>
+<td>The <code>client_id</code> or <code>client_secret</code> is missing or incorrect: <code>{"error": "invalid_client"}</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Invalid Scope</td>
+<td>A scope requested in the refresh was not part of the original grant: <code>{"error": "invalid_scope"}</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>Unsupported Grant Type</td>
+<td>The <code>grant_type</code> parameter is not one of <code>authorization_code</code> or <code>refresh_token</code>: <code>{"error": "unsupported_grant_type"}</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+</tbody></table>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Authorization/Cross-Origin-Resource-Sharing" data-section-id="tag/Authorization/Cross-Origin-Resource-Sharing" class="sc-dcJsrY eVrqat"><div class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-dhKdcB ilvzMQ"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Authorization/Cross-Origin-Resource-Sharing" aria-label="tag/Authorization/Cross-Origin-Resource-Sharing"></a>Cross Origin Resource Sharing</h2></div></div><div class="sc-fqkvVR bXmbgy"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct redoc-markdown "><blockquote>
+<p>CORS headers example:</p>
+</blockquote>
+<pre><code class="language-shell">$ <span class="token function">curl</span> https://api.todoist.com/api/v1/sync <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-H</span> <span class="token string">"Authorization: Bearer 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567"</span> <span class="token punctuation">\</span>
+    <span class="token parameter variable">-H</span> <span class="token string">"Origin: http://example.com"</span>
+
+HTTP/1.1 <span class="token number">200</span> OK
+Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://example.com
+Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,OPTIONS
+Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Authorization,Content-Type
+</code></pre>
+<p>All API endpoints not related to the initial OAuth2 flow support Cross Origin Resource
+Sharing (CORS) for requests from any origin. The <code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin</code> header
+echoes the request's <code>Origin</code>, and is set on every response, including error responses.
+<code>Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true</code> is sent only for Todoist's own browser origins.</p>
+</div></div></div><div id="tag/Authorization/operation/migrate_personal_token_api_v1_access_tokens_migrate_personal_token_post" data-section-id="tag/Authorization/operation/migrate_personal_token_api_v1_access_tokens_migrate_personal_token_post" class="sc-dcJsrY kNjBFu"><div data-section-id="operation/migrate_personal_token_api_v1_access_tokens_migrate_personal_token_post" id="operation/migrate_personal_token_api_v1_access_tokens_migrate_personal_token_post" class="sc-kAyceB XMnSL"><div class="sc-fqkvVR hARFxy"><h2 class="sc-jXbUNg kCMUHi"><a class="sc-jlZhew jrsfjb" href="https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1/#tag/Authorization/operation/migrate_personal_token_api_v1_access_tokens_migrate_personal_token_post" aria-label="tag/Authorization/operation/migrate_personal_token_api_v1_access_tokens_migrate_personal_token_post"></a>Migrate Personal Token </h2><div class="sc-bVVIoq bxAVse"><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct"><p>Tokens obtained via the old email/password authentication method can be
+migrated to the new OAuth access token. Migrating your users' personal tokens
+will allow users to see your app in their Todoist Settings page and give them
+the ability to manage their app authorization.</p>
+<p>A successful response has <code>200 OK</code> status and <code>application/json</code> Content-Type.</p>
+</div></div><h5 class="sc-dAlyuH hNlDMA">Request Body schema: <span class="sc-cWSHoV TDHxu">application/json</span><div class="sc-Nxspf sc-hRJfrW sc-ecPEgm lmPAIU gEdCms gckpsV">required</div></h5><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt guWXct"></div><table class="sc-dAbbOL ffxubm"><tbody><tr class=""><td class="sc-dLMFU sc-eldPxv hAsdv bPwHtV" kind="field" title="client_id"><span class="sc-gFqAkR jGHMtm"></span><span class="property-name">client_id</span><div class="sc-Nxspf sc-hRJfrW lmPAIU gEdCms">required</div></td><td class="sc-fPXMVe kDQoiR"><div><div><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-cfxfcM lmPAIU dZJSij"></span><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-gFAWRd lmPAIU jtxbJJ">string</span><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-gmPhUn lmPAIU cJOBjd"> (Client Id) </span></div> <div><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt jhfDPr"><p>The unique Client ID of the Todoist application that you registered.</p>
+</div></div></div></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="sc-dLMFU sc-eldPxv hAsdv bPwHtV" kind="field" title="client_secret"><span class="sc-gFqAkR jGHMtm"></span><span class="property-name">client_secret</span><div class="sc-Nxspf sc-hRJfrW lmPAIU gEdCms">required</div></td><td class="sc-fPXMVe kDQoiR"><div><div><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-cfxfcM lmPAIU dZJSij"></span><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-gFAWRd lmPAIU jtxbJJ">string</span><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-gmPhUn lmPAIU cJOBjd"> (Client Secret) </span></div> <div><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt jhfDPr"><p>The unique Client Secret of the Todoist application that you registered.</p>
+</div></div></div></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="sc-dLMFU sc-eldPxv hAsdv bPwHtV" kind="field" title="personal_token"><span class="sc-gFqAkR jGHMtm"></span><span class="property-name">personal_token</span><div class="sc-Nxspf sc-hRJfrW lmPAIU gEdCms">required</div></td><td class="sc-fPXMVe kDQoiR"><div><div><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-cfxfcM lmPAIU dZJSij"></span><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-gFAWRd lmPAIU jtxbJJ">string</span><span class="sc-Nxspf sc-gmPhUn lmPAIU cJOBjd"> (Personal Token) </span></div> <div><div class="sc-eeDRCY sc-eBMEME gvJSKt jhfDPr"><p>Token obtained from the email/password authentication.</p>
